<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org734513f">
<p>
Hello everyone,
</p>

<p>
I am happy to announce <a href=3D"https://github.com/LexiFi/dead_code_analy=
zer/releases">2 releases of the dead_code_analyzer</a>  (available via <cod=
e>opam</code>) :
</p>

<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li>Release <a href=3D"https://github.com/LexiFi/dead_code_analyzer/release=
s/tag/1.2.1">1.2.1</a> includes a collection of bug fixes and strengthens s=
emantics. This release is compatible with <b>OCaml 5.3</b>.</li>

<li>Release <a href=3D"https://github.com/LexiFi/dead_code_analyzer/release=
s/tag/1.3.0">1.3.0</a> is an update of 1.2.1, which extends the support to =
the range <b>OCaml 4.14 - 5.5</b>. There are a few known result inconsisten=
cies between OCaml &lt;=3D 5.2 and &gt;=3D 5.3, tracked in <a href=3D"https=
://github.com/LexiFi/dead_code_analyzer/issues/103">this issue</a>. They mo=
stly affect the optional arguments sections.
Because OCaml 4.14 is supported by this release 1.3.0, the dedicated branch=
 that was <a href=3D"https://github.com/fantazio/dead_code_analyzer/tree/4.=
14">available on my fork</a> will be deleted.</li>
</ul>

<p>
Thanks to David Maison, @sim642, @kit-ty-kate, and @nojb for their contribu=
tions, reviews, and feedback.
Thanks to <a href=3D"https://www.lexifi.com/">LexiFi</a> for its funding!
</p>

<p>
If you have used/use the dead_code_analyzer, I would love to hear about you=
r experience and usage. Feel free to post here, send me a DM, or an email a=
t <a href=3D"mailto:corentin@fantazio.eu">corentin@fantazio.eu</a>. It woul=
d help prioritize future developments and I might summarise the feedback in=
 an article, a presentation or the documentation.
</p>

<p>
If you encounter any issue with these releases, please <a href=3D"https://g=
ithub.com/LexiFi/dead_code_analyzer/issues">report it on the github reposit=
ory</a>.
Feedback and contributions are welcome.
</p>
